== Biography ==

Margaret Morris married [[Glasgow-437|Matthew Glasgow]] about 1865 in Lanarkshire, Scotland. Their son [[Glasgow-3579|John Glasgow]] was born in 1866; a Scottish birth index also names Margaret Morris as the mother of their son Matthew in 1873.<ref>"Scotland, Births and Baptisms, 1564–1950," FamilySearch, [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:FQG3-RYK entry for Matthew Glasgow, 1873], naming mother Margaret Morris.</ref>

Margaret's two former profiles gave approximate birth years of 1842 and 1846, without a cited birth record to settle the difference. The earlier profile placed her birth in New Monkland, Lanarkshire; the later one listed Airdrie but incorrectly assigned it to Fife. The earlier profile gives her death as 13 January 1928 at Blackridge, West Lothian; the later profile agrees on the year and place. These details need confirmation from the civil registers.

A family tree handed down to [[Glasgow-933|M Glasgow]] is the stated basis for part of the earlier profile. Its claims are retained here as family information pending verification.<ref>Unsourced family tree handed down to [[Glasgow-933|M Glasgow]], cited in the former Morris-48808 profile.</ref>

